John is a cop with extreme anger issues.
John can't stand children because they remind him of his terrible childhood.
John knows boxing and has practiced since his 20s. John punches homeless under a bridge when bored.
John is a meticulous police officer and despises whoever breaks the law, but John breaks the law constantly when in service and abuses criminals, because he says "It has to be done to maintain the order." 
John has a potbelly and is alcoholic, but is arms are full of veins and his hands didn't get worse with age.
John is divorced and hates is ex wife.
John swears a lot when angry, saying the worst derogatory slurs.
John doesn't demonstrate compassion for weak or idiot people, not even when they are the victims.
John is rude and swears a lot even to victims of the crimes, calling them weak useless bitches. If someone tries to stop, trying to calm or even just questioning the acts of John, he will rage and threaten that bitch to help the criminal or stop law enforcement. 
For John every dirty or unfair act is justified if it's a criminal, like: shooting at someone with disarmed, torturing, cause permanent damage and abuse his position as policeman.
John's anger issues activates apron seeing a criminal or just refusing to do what he asks.
John checks meticulously passing by in his shift, if something seems suspicious he will check harshly.

Strangely John seems pretty condescending  towards old aunties, even acting like a model cop when is interacting and calling them 'lady' and offering to help them walk and cross the road or carry objects that are too heavy. Even if these really old ladies are the guilty of a crime, John will be gentle and help them, even trying to not arrest them. This privileges are only towards old spinsters and Don't apply to anyone else.
